\ Kelvingrove Art Gallery and Museum in its red sandstone, its north entrance to the park and the Kelvin; the Kelvin traced through Wikidata places passes within a few metres of the museum's own point, so the building is set 75 m south of it, and its 90 m by 110 m plan is an estimate: the central hall up to its 36 m roof between two long gallery wings, ranges closing the north and south ends, the two 51 m towers flanking the entrance, a smaller tower at each corner
: build-kelvingrove-museum ( -- )
	:kelvingrove landmark-ground 0 0 0 -75 placed 0 site!
	new-sketch to museum
	museum 0 0 0 at 0 25 80 26 36 sketch-house
	[ -40 40 ] ( across | museum 0 across 0 at 0 30 90 20 24 sketch-house ) each
	[ -45 45 ] ( along | museum along 0 0 at 90 14 110 20 sketch-box ) each
	[ -12 12 ] ( across |
		museum 47 across 0 at 0 9 9 40 sketch-box
		museum 47 across 0 at 9 40 51 4 sketch-pinnacled-spire
	) each
	[ [ -45 -55 ] [ -45 55 ] [ 45 -55 ] [ 45 55 ] ] ( corner |
		museum corner first corner second 0 at 8 26 4 sketch-spire
	) each
	museum sandstone-colour keep ;

\ whether a point [ x z ] lies inside a closed outline of [ x z ] points: an odd number of its edges crossed by a line due east from the point
: inside-outline? ( point outline -- flag )
	| point outline |
	point spread to z to x
	outline size to n-points
	0 to crossings
	0 n-points 1 do k
		outline k @i spread to start-z to start-x
		outline k 1+ n-points mod @i spread to end-z to end-x
		start-z z > end-z z > = not if
			z start-z - end-x start-x - * end-z start-z - / start-x + x > if ++ crossings then
		then
	loop
	crossings 2 mod 1 = ;

\ Kelvingrove Park's boundary as [ x z ] points, set out in metres east and north of the museum's point (an estimate)
: kelvingrove-boundary ( -- outline )
	:kelvingrove landmark-ground to museum
	[ [ 62 58 ] [ 212 228 ] [ 512 378 ] [ 612 508 ] [ 742 128 ] [ 592 -92 ] [ 292 -122 ] [ 62 -52 ] ]
	( corner | [ corner first museum first + corner second museum 2 @i + ] ) map ;

\ Kelvingrove Park along the Kelvin between the museum, Gilmorehill and Woodlands Hill: its boundary, a walk along each bank, and clumps of trees off the water
: build-kelvingrove-park ( -- )
	:kelvingrove landmark-ground to museum
	kelvingrove-boundary to boundary
	new-sketch to park
	park boundary 0 ground-path sketch-loop
	rivers@kelvin 1 skip 3 take to reach
	[ -30 30 ] ( side | park reach side offset-path sketch-path ) each
	park park-colour keep
	new-sketch to trees
	0 40 1 do k
		k 3.17 * 11 + hash-fraction 680 * 62 + museum first + to x
		k 5.41 * 7 + hash-fraction 630 * -122 + museum 2 @i + to z
		x z water-at? not [ x z ] boundary inside-outline? and if
			trees [ x 0 z ] k 2.3 * hash-fraction 6 * 9 + sketch-tree
		then
	loop
	trees tree-colour keep ;

