\ Orkney: Kirkwall's streets lined with buildings an estimated 10 m high; St Magnus Cathedral in its red sandstone, 50 m to the spire's tip (published), its nave, transepts and crossing tower estimates; the ruins of the Bishop's and the Earl's palaces beside it; the naval base's oil tanks at Lyness; the Old Man of Hoy, a stack 137 m high (published) about 30 m across; the Ring of Brodgar, 27 stones on a circle about 100 m across; the Kitchener Memorial on Marwick Head; Hatston and Skeabrae are among the airfields (the sizes not given as published are estimates)
