\ the battleship Tirpitz in March 1942, 251 m long overall, 241.6 m at the waterline, 36 m in the beam (published): the hull from the waterline to the deck with its sheer; the four twin 38 cm turrets, Anton and Bruno forward, Caesar and Dora aft, Bruno and Caesar superfiring, their barrels 17.9 m (47 calibres, published); the six twin 15 cm turrets, three a side, barrels 8.3 m (55 calibres); the eight twin 10.5 cm mounts, barrels 6.8 m (65 calibres); the conning tower and the tower mast with the main rangefinder across its top; the funnel and its cap; the four SL-8 directors' domes; the hangars and the double-ended catapult across the deck with an Arado on it (published as fitted), the boat cranes; the mainmast and the after superstructure with its rangefinder; trees cut and laid on her deck as camouflage (reported). Every position and every height above the deck is an estimate from drawings
