\ the anchorage in Fættenfjord in March 1942: the Tirpitz and two destroyers of her escort moored ahead of and astern of her behind the anti-torpedo nets, the nets running from the shore round the seaward side of all three, a float every 15 m; the smoke generators that hid the ship in artificial fog, drums along the shore behind her; four light flak positions on the shore above her, each a ring of sandbags round a gun pointing over the water (the nets, the fog, the flak and the escort reported; the layout an estimate). The shore is on her left, the side she lies against
