\ the German destroyers' wrecks by Narvik on 28 May 1940 whose positions are recorded to the second, both run ashore and blown up by their crews on 13 April: Z2 Georg Thiele in Rombaksbotn, broken in two, her bow on the shore (OpenStreetMap's wreck, which still shows), and Z19 Hermann Künne in Trollvika in the Herjangsfjord (Wikidata); drawn with the destroyer's shape, the length above the water estimates
